title The helper that was already lifted, and a fall predicted before it was measured
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, read one council-rota row, send as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. REDS %142, %143, %144 all read CLOSED in crux/REDS.md, so no red stood open and the line was clear for constructive work.
think The running thread came off the top three rows of session-logs/README.md and the newest recommend line -- elder_waits named as the next honest head after the meter repair that ended the prior lap.
think Council rota row: 183 caravan laps counted by git log --oneline --grep="caravan:" | wc -l, so 183 mod 5 = 3, the Water/Venus row -- Gall's Law, the happy zone and the thin edge, growing a language. Every one of the three argues growing a system from a working smaller one, which is exactly the lift-underneath shape this lap needed.
think Priced the family before touching it. sh tools/fixtures/ladder_reach_visibility_scan.sh elder_waits read fifty-one identical fifteen-line bodies, forty-eight above the fold line, widens=53 split forty-eight function openings of a private waits and five openings of a private Table.
think The correctness question the meter cannot ask: a lifted body reaching waits(rung, ...) in the harness runs the HARNESS waits, so every folding rung's own waits must already be that same body. Checked all forty-three by comparing each rung's waits body against the delegating stub text -- all forty-three matched, and withdraw.rye's differing waits (!table.taken and !table.gone) sits among the eight staying home anyway.
think Computed the honest fall from the scan's own formula before editing: copies 51, lines 15, stub 3, folding 43, held 8, so (51-1)*15 - ((43-1)*3 + 7*15) = 519. The scan prints 579 because it prices all forty-eight above the line.
obs The carry measured 63,964 -> 63,445 after the lift -- exactly 519. A formula that predicts its own next reading is a meter the fold queue can be ordered on.
obs The lift widened nothing on either side. waits was lifted a lap earlier, so the forty-eight function openings the meter priced were a cost on one ordering of the work rather than a cost at all; turn_bit stood public in all forty-three before this lap arrived. Two lifts running have now found the same answer, which makes it a shape rather than a coincidence.
obs The five private-Table rungs were paid by leaving them home with their whole bodies. Publishing a record type five rungs chose to keep buys 75 lines and spends a boundary five modules drew on purpose; the boundary is worth more.
obs Two prose guards fired on this lap's own new sentences and both were right. The harness-prose guard refused a doc line naming the harness parameter, and the recited-count guard refused a GREEN line saying fifty-three once the fold made that number unfindable in the file printing it. Each sentence was rewritten to name the shape rather than the guard loosened to admit the number.
obs One honest tightening rode along: the reach witness pinned SINK_ABOVE rung=serve.rye holds=3, which contains also matched against the live 38. A prefix that matches a superset is an assert that cannot fail, so it now reads 38.
